	abstract = {Terahertz (THz) communication has become one of the high-proﬁle technologies in the sixth generation (6G) mobile communication networks due to its huge bandwidth and ultra-high data transmission rate. In this paper, the resource allocation algorithm for indoor THz networks is investigated and a problem is formulated to maximize the spectral efﬁciency (SE). The optimization problem is decomposed into two sub-problems including sub-band allocation problem and power allocation problem. In the ﬁrst stage, the sub-band allocation problem is solved using Hungarian algorithm based on the Long-UserCentral-Window (LUCW) principle. In the second stage, the sequential quadratic programming (SQP) algorithm is used to obtain the optimal power allocation. Finally, simulation results show that the proposed algorithm has higher SE comparing with some conventional schemes.},
